#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e8e6cf-6f2d-52c7-9466-9bfe3b894881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}4 \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552786} {:answer/id #uuid "65b7db08-9576-514c-8058-8a41c58bbf69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552807} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8131b6-7baf-5780-9fa9-322bc7065bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}t \\left(8 t^{3} + 8\\right) \\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552821} {:answer/id #uuid "8fba40cf-cdeb-5e12-8408-18012db7f78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552824} {:answer/id #uuid "9370dc17-2d30-55db-b451-380c43d516d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{4 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552825}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552824} :answer-field/id #uuid "26a99906-0888-518b-a404-298ec7ba3467" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "add2d24a-5255-5b7c-82c3-e44bf8b960be" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C 4 x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=2 y^{3} + 2$ traversed between the points $(4,1)$ and $(130,4)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the parameter $y=t.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y).$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 t^{3} + 2.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\langle 2 t^{3} + 2,\\,t\\rangle,\\quad 1\\le t\\le 4\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le 4$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{3} + 2)i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)j \\\\ &=(6 t^{2})i+j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(6 t^{2})^2+1^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} y,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=4\\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2}t^{1} \\\\ &=4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 4 x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{4}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{4}(4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{4}4 t \\left(2 t^{3} + 2\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124cbff1-5e98-5d16-ab1f-cc5dd9bcb262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}4 t^{2} \\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552784} {:answer/id #uuid "73be819e-c547-5ed8-8ad1-7fbb722f68d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{4}4 t^{2} \\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552811} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8d803f-dbce-540f-ae8b-e4bb8ad0e1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}4 \\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552822} {:answer/id #uuid "b95ec9fe-f64a-57bc-b94e-843559920235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}4 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552835} {:answer/id #uuid "e4084919-f343-5591-a6f6-3cbf2ccd120c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}4 \\sqrt{5} t^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552844}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552784} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec0c910-12f6-5049-8da0-f391acb979fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da6a50f8-dbf0-5c57-9f91-2fc2ad40dfd3" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C 4 y e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $\\frac{x}{2}=\\ln y$ traversed between the points $(0,1)$ and $(4,e^{2})$.\n\n*Hint: Use the parameter $y=t.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve can be expressed in the form $x=x(y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=\\ln y\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,x=2 \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\langle 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)},\\,t\\rangle,\\quad 1\\le t\\le e^{2}\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $1\\le t\\le e^{2}$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)j \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)i+j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)^2+1^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{t^2}+1} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{t}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=4 y e^{x}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=4 y e^{x} \\\\ &=4\\cdot t^{1}e^{2\\ln t} \\\\ &=4\\cdot t^{1}\\left(t^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 4 y e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}(4 t^{3})\\cdot \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{4}{t^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{e^{2}}4 t^{2} \\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e8e17dd-b1fd-5b63-9132-ad3a7dd6d991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{9 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552797} {:answer/id #uuid "4f69e9c5-3b56-564c-bca3-98cc70036ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}t \\left(15 - 15 t^{3}\\right) \\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552804} {:answer/id #uuid "66347383-a7b3-50bf-9101-6c7215d0630b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552808} {:answer/id #uuid "8f161683-83c0-50bf-a17a-f24ed9e6c9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552823} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ca4202-33f0-5ef5-aa09-f8e692b0f39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}5 \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552829}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552823} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb5ae6c-eb61-510c-8183-96be18ef2c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e43f4bf4-b216-5205-b149-df3643df4708" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C 5 x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the section of the curve $x=3 - 3 y^{3}$ traversed between the points $(3,0)$ and $(-78,3)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the parameter $y=t.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $x=x(y).$ Therefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=x(t)=3 - 3 t^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\langle 3 - 3 t^{3},\\,t\\rangle,\\quad 0\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $0\\le t\\le 3$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 - 3 t^{3})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)j \\\\ &=(- 9 t^{2})i+j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(- 9 t^{2})^2+1^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=5 x^{2} y,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=5\\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2}t^{1} \\\\ &=5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 5 x^{2} y\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}(5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}5 t \\left(3 - 3 t^{3}\\right)^{2} \\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f303671-2e9e-5abb-8d28-bb66030b781a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553697} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac71fd6-aef4-521a-be30-ea15e9fd1d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553702} {:answer/id #uuid "79b7ae4b-a531-5e36-9642-7063e55bfd39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553705} {:answer/id #uuid "d73fd73f-0590-5f6f-a4f5-edc9dba1df7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553718} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7b0bc1-b548-5a45-8603-72e62b1d2cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553722}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553697} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1dbdc3-6266-50e7-8ca0-341d52ae8cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3f24b968-c90a-5088-b77c-2d14ff47db8f" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{8}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{2}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(8)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553704 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4524d28f-034a-5b7e-8273-1db28285d123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{81}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553694} {:answer/id #uuid "5343a329-7bfb-59e4-ae4b-2f0d39395b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553699} {:answer/id #uuid "537e318d-1b07-5122-a845-50ebd93fbfcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553700} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f1c439-a4cc-5191-9808-eb4900c85251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553709} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a08eda-5358-5633-8b81-3f6cde1d724a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553699} :answer-field/id #uuid "412c1719-c37c-55ff-a7da-39e301f8555b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "72794993-4291-5561-9810-697b71da5a36" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{9}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{2}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{9} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(9)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdd6321-be9a-530d-ad60-9434561f2fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553689} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0a7d28-abc6-5527-bf50-a694e4fbb4dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{81}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553696} {:answer/id #uuid "4f312f01-6782-5531-848e-0c1e08dec267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553698} {:answer/id #uuid "56c7bc55-7497-58e6-98f8-088e56c3bd16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553701} {:answer/id #uuid "be74edf5-4892-55ba-b89d-d422d71fe26f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553713}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553689} :answer-field/id #uuid "c382a319-9053-522a-af05-41d0f8f8fadb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80fdfeeb-1745-5bda-a2bf-003e2bea480c" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{9}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{7}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{9} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(9)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{7} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(7)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e83a1b-7c09-584f-89fe-d536701f2d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553690} {:answer/id #uuid "ae61fd26-957d-5457-962b-16a3d69306e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553710} {:answer/id #uuid "b2abdd01-f402-5a52-ad58-3efffea941c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553712} {:answer/id #uuid "ee4afd5f-eb46-5b6a-80e9-ddcf1dc087ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553721} {:answer/id #uuid "ff680fc3-ce64-528a-856e-7bfce2f117d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553723}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553712} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1b1e5-5a41-5916-bff2-9aa7ce4c5ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c5d09569-8769-5378-ac85-faeb959d3726" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{7}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{7} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(7)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a4eed1f-3af9-5976-b03d-acebc6d144a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553695} {:answer/id #uuid "94334901-fb74-5742-be6c-6a327b7ee13e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553708} {:answer/id #uuid "c21af765-fb6e-5349-8e2a-df0c6bd18fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{121}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553714} {:answer/id #uuid "cc606102-32d8-5ce3-b21a-bb23f9b354a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{11}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553717} {:answer/id #uuid "eb71c85d-2053-5194-ac88-087d8dcd6991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553695} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa59c2e-fd2e-57d5-9372-070e8785c69b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea3ff876-21d3-588e-bcef-ab512e92b202" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{11}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{4}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{11} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(11)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{121} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{4} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(4)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09332eae-5b2a-514b-8867-2093558d05b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\left(\\frac{7}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553770} {:answer/id #uuid "420c6f0f-9dce-576e-9b0d-e95c7499ccb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\left(\\frac{11}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553778} {:answer/id #uuid "776051fe-e8fa-5d70-877e-b7f12d71dc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\left(\\frac{14}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553782} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fa03e7-07e0-5b72-9c4a-d1951c6e832e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553790} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8388c4-b4b0-5c49-a3e6-c0618fd0f8f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553798}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553782} :answer-field/id #uuid "93450f91-e2e7-5d78-85f6-4f4af1e8b902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0da10636-70da-5542-b982-fb7b4f87a3a4" :question/problem "![](images/09/09a38bb4306728f97b7fecbf9ab1bda7aa957607352c1ab27af09489c271c3ed.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}9\\left({y}^{2}-2x\\right)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,1)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(1+t(3-1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1+2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9\\left({y}^{2}-2x\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =9\\left((1+2t)^{2}-2(2t)\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(1+4t+4{t}^{2}-4t\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(4{t}^{2}+1\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(2{[\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+t]}_{0}^{1}\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(2(\\frac{4}{3}+1)-2(0)\\right)\\\\  & =9\\left(\\frac{14}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0752d09c-5f6a-5f53-b2ee-4d14923c79a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553769} {:answer/id #uuid "618f68da-24b3-5f0a-805d-fbaacb6ec826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\frac{13}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553780} {:answer/id #uuid "83f08410-f8d4-5fcb-88cc-cce40721c333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\frac{15}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553783} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab18849-82d2-5380-bfc1-cc92cf4de014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553787} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5790a3-b0de-5077-a139-ed86ea6ba02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553780} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a51f296-5463-5808-9339-98064322cbb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "108f6b56-f476-502d-ac1b-82f7c7bee892" :question/problem "![](images/ab/ab95b870025708090e40cbd7645072e8f4453cf50047b2a00036a30171c81994.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}3\\left(\\sqrt{x-1}+y\\right)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(1,2)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(1,2)$ and $(2,1).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(1+t(2-1)),\\,(2+t(1-2))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+t,\\,2-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3\\left(\\sqrt{x-1}+y\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3\\left(\\sqrt{(1+t)-1}+2-t\\right)\\\\  & =3\\left(\\sqrt{t}-t+2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{t}-t+2)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =3\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{1/2}-t+2)\\,\\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =3\\left({[\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+2t]}_{0}^{1}\\right)\\\\  & =3\\left((\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+2)-(0)\\right)\\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{13}{6}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cbd8d3d-bf94-5248-baf7-04662b6aadb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left({e}^{2}+1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553775} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a00b88-cc53-5b01-b917-ddbe6814de6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(\\frac{3}{2}(e+1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553793} {:answer/id #uuid "e4284b1e-3a30-52a4-94c0-1caf9580e943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(\\frac{e}{2}-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553797} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e12e4a-0957-5b8e-85c2-01f0b3e26b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}(e-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553801} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc5da25-166a-5b6b-820b-9a27ca4a5b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(\\frac{1}{2}(e-1)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553801} :answer-field/id #uuid "efbebf4f-659b-5cc4-bb41-66562e488f37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2b42b22b-83d6-590d-b354-39580363db2b" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e5257867dae67451500793687a2da24ee31a73a17c691d8d8a6dcded46e8993.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}7\\left(x{e}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the three-quarters of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(3,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $3$ and $1,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=7\\left(x{e}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =7\\left((3\\operatorname{cos}t){e}^{1-\\operatorname{sin}^{2}t}\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(3\\operatorname{cos}t{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}^{2}t}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7\\left({\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}t{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}^{2}t})\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}t)\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}^{2}t}\\,\\text{d}t\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}^{2}t,$ $\\text{d}u=-2\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\left(-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}^{2}t}\\,\\text{d}t\\right)& =7\\left(-9{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,(-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}{e}^{u}{|}_{0}^{1}\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}[{e}^{1}-{e}^{0}]\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (e-1)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(\\frac{9}{2}(e-1)\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28779ab3-b956-50e6-818b-e6f98c82ef13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553773} {:answer/id #uuid "39e080af-d60a-5141-9d7b-170da955f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553776} {:answer/id #uuid "842f3d35-4a65-5fbb-a1f8-17b9bb34c7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553784} {:answer/id #uuid "aa31a872-ecbe-5369-ab2a-5b1f9b98b2a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(-6\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553788} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a561cd-3c03-570c-916f-6173a02ece12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(5\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553776} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee29c494-9956-584f-b89c-04ed9aab541e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d3f41fe-2ff6-5192-9b2b-6d5b3c48b78f" :question/problem "![](images/be/be3ad044a611d99e67c89d053d4878a2835be65828a4dc9300697bfd61822994.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}7\\left({x}^{2}y\\right)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the below-left quarter of the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(-1,0)$ to the point $(0,-2),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $2,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}t)=2\\operatorname{cos}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=7\\left({x}^{2}y\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =7\\left((\\operatorname{cos}t)^{2}(2\\operatorname{sin}t)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(2\\operatorname{sin}t{cos}^{2}t\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7\\left({\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{sin}t{cos}^{2}t)\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}t)\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}t{cos}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}t,$ $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\left(4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}t{cos}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t\\right)& =7\\left(4{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{u}^{3}\\,(-\\text{d}u)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(-4{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(-{u}^{4}{|}_{-1}^{0}\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(-[(0)^{4}-(-1)^{4}]\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(-(-1)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(1\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "688703f1-baed-5882-b609-dee232bef6a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553781} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7df652-c5bc-5ca9-bc05-48812058f7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553785} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ecac19-efd7-59bf-a437-69523cb8f1cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553792} {:answer/id #uuid "d6390df0-7054-59fa-85ef-6b7ce29f20c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(8\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553795} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9c1463-2e33-5db8-a497-c62cd8d39bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\left(12\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553792} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae189165-2609-5ae1-b76b-109d1c7e5259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c44f9146-1b6c-5fb1-ad95-4b025e298a3e" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d83f771aa650879909c33d7033e80ca044b7e6f8369e19667e6173aa8a40737.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}7\\left(x+\\sqrt{3y}\\right)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(2,0)$ and $(0,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(2+t(0-2)),\\,(0+t(3-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-2t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=7\\left(x+\\sqrt{3y}\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =7\\left((2-2t)+\\sqrt{3(3t)}\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(2-2t+3\\sqrt{t}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7\\left({\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-2t+3\\sqrt{t})\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-2t+3{t}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}t\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(3{[2t-{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{1}\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(3[(2(1)-(1)^{2}+2(1)^{3/2})-(0)]\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(3(3)\\right)\\\\  & =7\\left(9\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e471b01c-8372-5dbf-b0df-5b3453e6100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}\\left(-1+4\\sqrt{6}\\right)-\\sqrt{29}\\left(-1+4\\sqrt{6}\\right)}{\\sqrt{319}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554846}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554846} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9518c7-dd24-58bc-a206-4006d441dd9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4f0b1b9b-0863-5cb2-867f-94ad474fb844" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨\\sqrt{6},2,-1⟩$ and $b=⟨4,-2,-3⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{6})(4)+(2)(-2)+(-1)(-3)}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-4+3}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+4\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{29}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{b}_{x}{a}_{x}+{b}_{y}{a}_{y}+{b}_{z}{a}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+4\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+4\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{-1+4\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{29}}-\\frac{-1+4\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}\\left(-1+4\\sqrt{6}\\right)-\\sqrt{29}\\left(-1+4\\sqrt{6}\\right)}{\\sqrt{319}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9b48b0-d97f-58e4-9020-b27a2d4f3d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554819} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb04077-d22e-5117-b194-0f0acf1d352d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}+2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{80}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554831} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5683dd-3b44-569f-9184-b9a9dd913da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{30}-2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{80}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554832} {:answer/id #uuid "a38f036c-5867-564b-8d07-e1b6b83b524f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554834} {:answer/id #uuid "e97936bc-ddbb-5b82-994c-9bbad040900c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}-2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{80}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554847}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554847} :answer-field/id #uuid "db09d6ae-d98a-5518-8809-069b4c1aee1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3e4b28c-e8a8-5cbb-89ef-d351d2bc4c04" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-\\sqrt{3},-\\sqrt{6},1⟩$ and $b=⟨-1,1,\\sqrt{6}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\sqrt{3})(-1)+(-\\sqrt{6})(1)+(1)(\\sqrt{6})}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{b}_{x}{a}_{x}+{b}_{y}{a}_{y}+{b}_{z}{a}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{6})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{30}-2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{80}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3008eecb-dd1f-56ce-9019-7b10e3694893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554822} {:answer/id #uuid "3dbe5db7-75f9-5a77-b537-b1a09cc57e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554824} {:answer/id #uuid "46374ed0-5dc9-5f91-a8d1-bd7992f47ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}-4\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{200}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554826} {:answer/id #uuid "d309d8da-6af7-57bb-b7ea-1d4bce7cb08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}+4\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{200}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554840} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b4caf3-f064-58e4-810d-38b21051f146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}+4\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{200}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554840} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab1bd42b-9b4a-500f-a3fe-01ffe62acb76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d2188174-52cd-511b-87a0-828e4b888f06" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,-\\sqrt{3},4⟩$ and $b=⟨-\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{6},\\sqrt{2}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a+{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(-\\sqrt{2})+(-\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{6})+(4)(\\sqrt{2})}{\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(\\sqrt{6})^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+4\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{b}_{x}{a}_{x}+{b}_{y}{a}_{y}+{b}_{z}{a}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{20}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a+{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}+4\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{200}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2256bc8f-16a5-5763-9ff1-4dffbeae3f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{\\sqrt{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554821} {:answer/id #uuid "31ba76c7-5b61-52e2-8626-7c128445a699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right)-(2\\sqrt{2}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right))}{\\sqrt{120}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554823} {:answer/id #uuid "c624c424-e407-59d8-b6d8-5d60cf147b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right)+(2\\sqrt{2}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right))}{\\sqrt{120}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554838} {:answer/id #uuid "d311c211-ba0b-574c-b6f7-1faff00bc1fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{15}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right)-(2\\sqrt{2}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right))}{\\sqrt{120}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554841} {:answer/id #uuid "ef54b90c-8daf-5b9c-bdc2-f56a5c5c5ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{\\sqrt{8}}-\\left(\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{15}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554823} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f521ab9-1ddd-5450-85ba-9420283060bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d9750954-2644-5f46-9bc3-7cd5fcb4219c" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨3,\\sqrt{5},1⟩$ and $b=⟨-1,-\\sqrt{3},2⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(-1)+(\\sqrt{5})(-\\sqrt{3})+(1)(2)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-\\sqrt{15}+2}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{\\sqrt{8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{b}_{x}{a}_{x}+{b}_{y}{a}_{y}+{b}_{z}{a}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\sqrt{15}-1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =-\\frac{1+\\sqrt{15}}{\\sqrt{8}}-\\left(-\\frac{1+\\sqrt{15}}{\\sqrt{15}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right)-(2\\sqrt{2}\\left(-\\sqrt{15}-1\\right))}{\\sqrt{120}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fea03f7-25d3-517e-9cc2-81572e335e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right)+(\\sqrt{31}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right))}{\\sqrt{558}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554825} {:answer/id #uuid "5ef9a9d5-a739-56b2-9661-ac1056cf1fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{31}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554829} {:answer/id #uuid "7531ab09-81e4-58af-afd3-fb322d27c79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right)-(\\sqrt{31}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right))}{\\sqrt{558}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554830} {:answer/id #uuid "a18083e1-382f-5d93-afe5-ff52c2b3cc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\left(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right)-(\\sqrt{31}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right))}{\\sqrt{558}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554833} {:answer/id #uuid "e10defb3-8236-5ae1-b347-1f178892fd43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{31}}-\\left(\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{18}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554845}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554830} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f3ed2bb-7c5c-5d4f-8584-c6f1cbf01e87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "de71841a-f8e7-51cc-a207-4dfd1f658c74" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨\\sqrt{3},3,-\\sqrt{6}⟩$ and $b=⟨-3,-4,-\\sqrt{6}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})(-3)+(3)(-4)+(-\\sqrt{6})(-\\sqrt{6})}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-\\sqrt{6})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\sqrt{3}-12+6}{\\sqrt{31}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{31}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{b}_{x}{a}_{x}+{b}_{y}{a}_{y}+{b}_{z}{a}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{6})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-3\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{18}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}+6}{\\sqrt{31}}-\\left(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}+6}{\\sqrt{18}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right)-(\\sqrt{31}\\left(-6-3\\sqrt{3}\\right))}{\\sqrt{558}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b337fa7-bd8b-5c90-a0a9-70650e2fdcbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554860} {:answer/id #uuid "7d135ef6-116e-5934-84c1-11a47c59668f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554878} {:answer/id #uuid "836d5d14-56d9-58cb-9958-435971a6cb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554881} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf45132-d649-533a-9603-ef7dfcb122bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554884} {:answer/id #uuid "ce656dd1-358f-523e-9af0-50c385c018ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554904}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554884} :answer-field/id #uuid "46488809-31b0-5e06-a0e3-3b15d04132fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0de1e67b-08b0-590a-987d-98f0797e3256" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(4 - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4 - 4 t^{2},\\quad y=4 t^{2},\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(8 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(4\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 8 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(8 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 8 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(8 t\\right)+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 32 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 32 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 32 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 16 t^{2} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-16\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)]-[\\left(-16\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38d9f40b-294c-5d0d-b920-423d8a07b7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554864} {:answer/id #uuid "59829333-e505-5da3-98f2-21a5554e8c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554870} {:answer/id #uuid "9b006bad-ce48-5e7e-a06c-1c336b782ab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554888} {:answer/id #uuid "c0dc3100-368a-5fe9-8467-27205633130c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554902} {:answer/id #uuid "ed445195-4fe7-541a-8a1e-6f2a605ae973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554910} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d5efd9d-3e69-5f74-9f3d-3ac7e3057828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "348e1450-060b-511e-ab1c-9ac3626ec2eb" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 6 x + 5 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(5 t^{2} - 5 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t^{3} - 6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=5 t^{2} - 5 t,\\quad y=6 t^{3} - 6 t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- 6 x + 5 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(5 t^{2} - 5 t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(6 t^{3} - 6 t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(10 t - 5\\right)\\,i+\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(10 t - 5\\right)\\,i+\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(10 t - 5\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(300 t^{4} - 450 t^{3} + 150 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(10 t - 5\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(10 t - 5\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[60 t^{5} - \\frac{225 t^{4}}{2} + 50 t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(50\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{225}{2}\\right)+\\left(60\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =- \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "114cd428-9ff5-5378-aaf6-79f85ced9209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554854} {:answer/id #uuid "685f9e08-daff-5c3f-b9a5-c47f24d86c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554873} {:answer/id #uuid "9e82d924-eb43-5d3a-931f-13fe24c0e9e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554889} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ebf419-c2bb-56d3-aef3-a83b86af5ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554893} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8d6487-1209-5a0b-84d1-1ff1578aaccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554898}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554854} :answer-field/id #uuid "32b499d6-e35b-5df6-b9cc-4a94b51e5a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4133c25f-bd85-507a-8e90-bf61f17f7c85" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(3 - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 - 3 t^{2},\\quad y=3 t^{2},\\quad z=4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(3\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(3\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(3\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 6 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(6 t\\right)+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 18 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 16 \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 18 t - 8 \\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 18 t - 8 \\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 9 t^{2} + 4 \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-9\\right)+\\left(4\\right)]-[\\left(-9\\right)+\\left(4\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5603107d-9563-57f2-ba74-697614f507d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554868} {:answer/id #uuid "691dd10a-c57a-5d20-99c1-541d1fc7c15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554874} {:answer/id #uuid "9f75d586-ec9d-5bbd-9ed9-a2cb0af7b409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 24 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554890} {:answer/id #uuid "bab50ed0-e1ba-597a-9fae-6f0bc3a2cefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554899} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9ac4e6-bfaf-5b63-9e0a-7f43b911ffbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554911} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c07df69-ac22-576f-bdf1-ec7b4560369b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "551d4d7b-a286-5922-9bb8-28fd2d1e93e0" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(y\\right)\\,i+\\left(x\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\pi).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad z=2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(y\\right)\\,i+\\left(x\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(12 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 12 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =12 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left(12 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ & =[\\left(0\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18df830f-ab86-5425-9738-33adc7144a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554857} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2f5870-6bef-5a74-bac7-cea2f02dad0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554879} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe93c39-19b8-5993-86a0-832c5694d298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554900} {:answer/id #uuid "bf92e1c7-9d7c-59ca-9b8b-0d362f20d0bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554901} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3c9e86-4f1e-5d6f-beb8-32c3b7b03702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554909} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fe68d1-7c6d-53bc-9521-f981d69d8bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "62239d5b-2148-5cb6-b90b-702d31af6174" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(2 - 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 - 2 t^{2},\\quad y=2 t^{2},\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 - 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(2\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 t\\right)+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 8 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 8 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 4 t^{2} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)]-[\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592